-- Commands read out of the mapdb's Ruby. Generated by `codex extract`.
--
-- 1631 edges extracted, 153 left alone.
--
-- Ending in `move 'X'` is not enough to extract one. Silverwood's door
-- reads `;e $SILVERWOOD_TOWN=:imt;move 'go door'`, and taking `go door`
-- from it discards which of four rooms the door leads back to -- and the
-- door needs club membership besides, which no client can observe. So an
-- unrecognised body means the edge is skipped and recorded below with its
-- reason, and an understood-but-unpublishable one is recorded as excluded:
-- a missing edge fails to route, a wrong one routes a character somewhere
-- they did not ask to go.

